 #uuid "3d43ba6e-0f3b-545b-8a27-3e657530e6fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442198 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe given sequence is a geometric sequence with the common ratio \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $|r|>1$, the sequence diverges." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442199 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442199 #edb/ref 1069 "q-141391" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442199 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442199 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following geometric sequence:\n\n$$\n2,\\,8,\\,32,\\,128,\\,…\n$$\n\nDetermine whether the sequence is convergent or divergent. If it converges, find the limit." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442199 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "45ac4819-8cd9-51ec-b2a8-2a52c6be8c3d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442199 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe  given sequence is a geometric sequence with the common ratio \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{8}{2}=4.\n$$\n\nSince $|r|=4>1,$ the sequence diverges." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442200 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442200 #edb/ref 1069 "q-495